removeRedundancy -- removes redundancies from a list of planes
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        removeRedundancy L
  * Inputs:
      * L, of pairs indexing affine planes
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, with no redundancies in L.

Description
===========

The method takes a list of pairs that indexes planes and removes redundancies
in the list.  By a redundancy, we mean when one plane in the list is contained
in another plane.



+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                      |
|                                        |
|o1 = R                                  |
|                                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                     |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x*y,y*z)                 |
|                                        |
|o2 = ideal (x*y, y*z)                   |
|                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of R                         |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = quasidegrees(R^1/I)            |
|                                        |
|o3 = {{0, {| 1 |}}, {0, {| 1 |, | 1 |}}}|
|                                        |
|o3 : List                               |
+----------------------------------------+

The two pairs in Q each correspond to the complex plane so there is a
redundancy.



+--------------------------+
|i4 : removeRedundancy Q   |
|                          |
|o4 = {{0, {| 1 |, | 1 |}}}|
|                          |
|o4 : List                 |
+--------------------------+

Ways to use removeRedundancy:
=============================

  * "removeRedundancy(List)"

